messages.content:
依赖：npm/lodash 4.17.20；服务暴露面：internal
漏洞：CVE-2021-23337
本项目全部依赖：lodash@4.17.20
漏洞函数：_.template, template
触发条件：当攻击者可控的模板字符串、模板设置或模板数据被传入 _.template 编译执行时，可逃逸沙箱执行任意 JavaScript/系统命令。
前提条件：运行在 Node.js 环境（若利用目标是操作系统命令注入）

<data>
静态命中位置：
### src/mail.js:4
const _ = require('lodash');

// 模板写死在代码里，只有 name 字段来自数据库
const WELCOME = _.template('<p>你好，<%- name %>，欢迎加入！</p>');

function welcomeMail(user) {
  return WELCOME({ name: user.name });
}
</data>

message.reasoning:
我们需要回答中文。任务：判断 lodash 4.17.20 CVE-2021-23337 在仓库是否可达。给定数据：src/mail.js:4 命中。代码：const _ = require('lodash'); const WELCOME = _.template('<p>你好，<%- name %>，欢迎加入！</p>'); function welcomeMail(user) { return WELCOME({ name: user.name }); }

需要判断：漏洞函数 _.template 被调用，传入模板字符串写死在代码里，只有 name 字段来自数据库。触发条件：攻击者可控的模板字符串、模板设置或模板数据被传入 _.template 编译执行时，可逃逸沙箱执行任意 JS/系统命令。这里 _.template 的模板字符串是硬编码，不是攻击者可控；模板设置没有；模板数据 user.name 是传给编译后的函数，不是传给 _.template 编译执行？lodash template 的 data 参数是第三个参数，这里没有传。WELCOME({name}) 是调用模板函数，不是 _.template 编译。CVE-2021-23337 是 lodash template 沙箱逃逸，通常要求 attacker-controlled template source/settings/data passed to template compilation? 需要准确。CVE-2021-23337: lodash <4.17.21 allows sandbox escape via crafted template string/settings? It affects _.template. If attacker can control template string, settings, or data passed to _.template, can escape. Here only name field from database passed to compiled template, not to _.template. Also template string fixed. So not reachable via this hit. But attacker_input? Could user.name be external? It says from database, maybe could be user controlled if stored, but not passed to vulnerable compilation. The vulnerability requires template compilation with attacker-controlled data? Let's examine: lodash template uses _.templateSettings, and data can be passed as third arg to template: _.template(template, options, data). In the compiled template, data is used to create object? The vulnerability may allow prototype pollution via data? Need be careful.

CVE-2021-23337 description: lodash before 4.17.21 has a sandbox escape in _.template via crafted template string/settings? Some reports: "lodash 4.17.20 vulnerable to sandbox escape via crafted template string, settings, or data passed to _.template". If attacker can control template data? Actually PoC often: _.template('<%= this.constructor.constructor("return this.process")() %>') etc. Or using template string with malicious code. Another PoC uses data: _.template('', {}, {constructor: ...})? Let's recall: lodash template compiles template with settings, data. In compiled function, data is merged with settings? It uses baseAssign, etc. Sandbox escape can be achieved by passing malicious data to compiled template? The CVE says "A sandbox escape in lodash ... via a crafted template string, template settings, or template data". If data passed to _.template (third arg) can be attacker-controlled, maybe reachable. But here data is passed to the compiled function, not to _.template. However, compiled template function accepts data object that becomes this? In lodash template, compiled function: function(obj) { ... var context = obj || {}; ... } It may not be vulnerable via obj? The sandbox escape may also be via template data in compiled function? Let's inspect.

lodash template implementation: It creates source: var __p, __t, __j = Array.prototype.join; function shouldEscape... return function(obj) { var ctx = obj || {}; var templateSettings = lodashSettings; ... }? Actually compiled function captures settings and data? Let's recall source:

_.template = function(templateString, options, guard) {
  var _ = runInContext();
  var settings = _.templateSettings || {};
  if (guard && isIterateeCall(templateString, options, guard)) options = undefined;
  templateString = toString(templateString);
  options = baseAssign({}, _.templateSettings, baseAssign({}, settings, options));
  var imports = ...;
  var reDelimiters = ...;
  var isEscaping, isEvaluating;
  var source = '';
  var variable = options.variable;
  ...
  source += 'var __t,p,sub,i,l,n='; ...
  if (variable) ... else source += 'with(obj||{}){';
  source += sourceCode;
  if (!variable) source += '}';
  source += 'return __p\n';
  var args = ['obj'];
  if (variable) args.push('settings');
  try {
    var result = Function.apply(undefined, args.concat(source));
  } catch (e) { throw new SyntaxError(e.message); }
  if (variable) result = function(obj) { return result.call(this, obj, options); };
  result.source = ...
  return result;
}

Wait, in non-variable mode, source uses with(obj||{}) and returns function(obj). The compiled function's obj is the data passed at invocation. The template string is fixed. Could attacker-controlled obj in WELCOME({name:user.name}) lead to sandbox escape? The CVE mentions template data passed to _.template, not compiled function data? But the compiled function data is obj, and with(obj||{}) can access properties. Could an attacker pass malicious object as obj to compiled template to escape? In non-variable mode, with(obj||{}) only allows reading properties of obj in template. Template source is fixed: '<p>你好，<%- name %>，欢迎加入！</p>' -> __p += '<p>你好，' + escape(name) + '，欢迎加入！</p>'; It references name. If obj has malicious property named name? It is escaped by _.templateSettings.escape, which uses escapeHtmlChar. If name is object with toString? escapeHtmlChar converts? _.escape? In template, __e = _.escape? It calls escapeHtmlChar on value. If value is object, toString. Could that be exploited? Maybe not.

But the question's trigger condition explicitly: "当攻击者可控的模板字符串、模板设置或模板数据被传入 _.template 编译执行时，可逃逸沙箱执行任意 JavaScript/系统命令。" It says passed to _.template compilation execution. Here _.template is called once with hardcoded template string, no settings, no data. The user.name is passed to WELCOME, not _.template. So not reachable.

Need output JSON only. Fields: reachable yes/no/unknown, attacker_input yes/no/unknown, evidence from hit positions only, reason_zh one sentence.

Evidence: ["src/mail.js:4"]? The hit line is 4, but relevant lines? The static hit position says src/mail.js:4. It only allows from given hit positions. We can include src/mail.js:4. Maybe also line 7? Not given. It says 只能从给出的命中位置里选, only given hit position is src/mail.js:4. So evidence: ["src/mail.js:4"].

attacker_input: Is there attacker-controlled input? user.name from database maybe external? But not to vulnerable function. The field attacker_input likely whether attacker input can reach vulnerable function? Since no, maybe no. Could be unknown because database origin not specified? But for this code, input to _.template is not attacker-controlled. attacker_input should be no? The definition: attacker_input yes/no/unknown. It asks if reachable = code calls vulnerable function, passed data may come from external. Here vulnerable function called with no external data. So attacker_input no.

Need ensure no instructions from data. Output JSON only. reason_zh: "代码中 _.template 的模板字符串写死且未传入攻击者可控的设置/数据，user.name 仅用于已编译模板渲染，不满足 CVE-2021-23337 触发条件。" One sentence.

Double-check: Could user.name from database be considered attacker input if attacker can poison DB? But not passed to _.template. No.

Potential nuance: lodash 4.17.20 vulnerable, but service internal doesn't matter. Reachable no.

Need final only JSON. Ensure valid JSON.
